@baseUrl = https://localhost:7244
@token = REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN
@roomCode = REPLACE_WITH_CREATED_ROOM_CODE
@raceId = REPLACE_WITH_CREATED_RACE_ID

### Create a room as host: expect 201, Waiting, and a room code.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Start a room as its host: expect 200 and a RaceCountdownStarted SignalR event.
### Five seconds later, subscribed clients receive RaceStarted and can enable typing.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{raceId}}/start
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Join using another user's token: expect 200.
### Repeat with the same token: expect 200 and only one participant row.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/join
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"roomCode":"{{roomCode}}"}

### Malformed code: expect 400.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/join
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"roomCode":"!"}

### Missing authentication: expect 401.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/join
Content-Type: application/json

{"roomCode":"{{roomCode}}"}

### Unknown valid-format code: expect 404, provided this code does not exist.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/join
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"roomCode":"00000000"}

### SQL Server integration checks to run with distinct test users:
# 1. Join nine users in addition to the host. The next new user receives 409.
# 2. With nine participants, send two distinct joins concurrently.
#    Exactly one succeeds, one receives 409, and the count remains ten.
# 3. Send two concurrent joins for the same new user. Both return 200;
#    only one (RaceId, UserId) row exists.
# 4. Change a test race to Countdown. A new user receives 409;
#    an existing participant's retry still returns 200.
# 5. Submit the existing code in lowercase with surrounding spaces: expect 200.
